credential.go adapts behavior from src/auth/{pat,tokens,scopes}.rs and
crates/webcodex-store/src/{accounts,models}.rs. The implementation language,
repository boundary, host-user identity projection, supported credential subset,
operational token-size bound and tests are modified for native Go integration.
See README.md for source references and differences from the original verifier.

../../repository/webcodex_api_key_repo.go and
../../../migrations/238_webcodex_api_keys.sql adapt the original api_keys record,
DDL and lifecycle from crates/webcodex-store/src/{accounts,models,schema}.rs.
Changes include PostgreSQL SQL, wc_ table namespace, existing host User foreign
key with canonical string auth projection, and atomic revoke UPDATE RETURNING.
See CREDENTIAL_STORAGE.md for the complete field and lifecycle source map.

../../server/webcodex_agent_tokens.go and ../protocol/agent_tokens.go adapt
src/runner_tokens_http.rs, src/runner_tokens_http/{routes,responses}.rs,
src/auth/{pat,scopes,middleware}.rs and src/route_metadata/account.rs.
../../repository/webcodex_agent_tokens.go adapts the managed lifecycle in
crates/webcodex-store/src/accounts.rs. Modifications include native panel-JWT
admin/self authorization using canonical immutable host IDs, bounded metadata
SQL, user/kind-scoped revoke, crypto/rand generation preserving original token
format, reuse of the configured Runner body bound, host backend-mode/rate-limit/
audit guards, whole-body audit omission and sanitized dependency errors.
Original account-credential collision lookup awaits that separate store/verifier.

jobs*.go additionally adapts crates/webcodex-runner-registry/src/{job_updates,
jobs,state,polling,reconciliation,access_control}.rs and core
{runner_job_lifecycle,runner_protocol,job_observation,audit_preview,sensitive_text}.rs.
The legacy structured-process slice adds native host Access APIs and authenticated
job_update mounting. Separate Job dispatch evidence, control registration and
bounded retained records replace synchronous waiter ownership. The reconciliation
slice adds atomic known-Job registration inventories, sequenced updates and log
snapshots, same-instance recovery with explicit host grace configuration and
cancellable deadline timers. Unknown-Job reconstruction and cross-instance durable
transfer remain refused. Legacy cursor replacement and optional sequence behavior
are preserved; dispatch-based stop and liveness gates are strengthened. README.md
records exact limits and incomplete source surfaces.

registry.go additionally classifies file_skill_read_file under the original
FileRead capability for synchronous polling, following the file operation in
crates/webcodex-core/src/runner_operation.rs:283-355 and the skill consumer in
src/tool_runtime/skills.rs:1234-1272. The Go adaptation preserves opaque content
and does not implement skill filesystem execution, a SkillStore, or MCP tools.
Registration still requires the complete original generation-2 baseline.

